Validation of the identifying assumption. With no capacity shock, no measurement noise and a reporting lag of zero, each institution is run on the base-year technology and its realised gross output is compared with the base-year output vector. The table reports, per mechanism, the ratio of realised to base-year output, the mean shortage rate, the maximum absolute accounting residual over all periods and the base-year reproduction error, on both the toy fixture and the real twenty-sector Eurostat substrate. All six ratios are 1.000000 and all six shortage rates are 0.000000, and cumulative welfare is 259.568805 for every mechanism but the dual track: the institutions agree exactly when information is perfect, which is what licenses the comparisons that follow.
